# Refund Desk: products and their stock, orders, and refunds decided by one rule.
# Data is kept in data/*.json between runs; every answer is JSON.

A Product has:
  Code is text
  Name is text
  Price is money
  Stock is whole number
  Never allow a negative stock
  Never allow a negative price

An Order has:
  Number is whole number
  Code is text
  Quantity is whole number
  Total is money
  Refunded is money

# What happens to a refund request.
A Refund is one of:
  Approved with order number as whole number and amount as money
  Review with order number as whole number and amount as money and reason as text
  Refused with order number as whole number and reason as text

Store products as a list of Product
Store orders as a list of Order
Store refunds as a list of Refund

Keep review limit at $100

# The refund rule, in one place: more than what is left is refused, a large refund goes to a person.
To decide refund:
  Receive order as Order and amount as money
  Set left to order's total - order's refunded
  When amount is more than left:
    Give a refused Refund with order number order's number and reason "Only {left} of order {order's number} can still be refunded."
  When amount is at least review limit:
    Give a review Refund with order number order's number and amount amount and reason "Refunds of {review limit} or more are checked by a person."
  Give an approved Refund with order number order's number and amount amount

To find product:
  Receive wanted as text
  Set found to products where code is wanted
  When found is empty:
    Stop with "There is no product {wanted}." and status 404
  Give found at 1

To product exists:
  Receive wanted as text
  Give the count of (products where code is wanted) is more than 0

To find order:
  Receive wanted as whole number
  Set found to orders where number is wanted
  When found is empty:
    Stop with "There is no order {wanted}." and status 404
  Give found at 1

When someone calls GET /products:
  Give products

When someone calls POST /products:
  Receive code as text and name as text and price as money and stock as whole number (0 if not given)
  When product exists with code:
    Stop with "There is already a product {code}." and status 409
  Add a Product with code code and name name and price price and stock stock to products
  Give the last of products with status 201

When someone calls POST /orders:
  Receive code as text and quantity as whole number
  When quantity is less than 1:
    Stop with "Order at least 1." and status 400
  Set product to find product with code
  When product's stock is less than quantity:
    Stop with "Only {product's stock} of {product's name} left." and status 409
  Set product's stock to product's stock - quantity
  Add an Order with number (the count of orders) + 1 and code code and quantity quantity and total product's price * quantity and refunded $0 to orders
  Give the last of orders with status 201

When someone calls GET /orders/{number}:
  Receive number as whole number
  Give find order with number

When someone calls POST /orders/{number}/refunds:
  Receive number as whole number and amount as money
  Set order to find order with number
  Set decision to decide refund with order and amount
  Add decision to refunds
  If decision is approved:
    Set order's refunded to order's refunded + decision's amount
  Give decision with status 201

When someone calls GET /refunds:
  Give refunds
